    "title": "Intensify descriptive imagery",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk2-adjective-repeat-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Intensify descriptive imagery",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Some learned adjectives repeat as AA or AABB for vivid description. Their reduplicated forms describe a quality; verb repetition instead softens an action. A monosyllabic adjective can repeat as AA, often with 的; this depicts a state and does not mean briefly trying an action, unlike verb repetition.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "他高高兴兴地回家。",
                "pinyin": "tā gāo gāo xìng xìng de huí jiā 。",
                "meaning": "He goes home cheerfully.",
                "audio": "b359cb73e68eeec6e485ce16d59b10c6ab68d65bec0de2c87021f5e3e8a9a1cc"
              },
              {
                "text": "孩子高高兴兴地上学。",
                "pinyin": "háizi gāo gāo xìng xìng de shàngxué 。",
                "meaning": "The child goes to school cheerfully.",
                "audio": "957e859b73214cdd515d5a9ecebdbdeba647321dbc7e17a078f468668f3e9880"
              },
              {
                "text": "你要好好的。",
                "pinyin": "nǐ yào hǎo hǎo de 。",
                "meaning": "You should be well and safe; 好好 depicts a good state.",
                "audio": "2134cf33022b307dde9f1acb52cdf2d372b144cf5cbea1b11e4ed8b98202e283"
              },
              {
                "text": "你看看。",
                "pinyin": "nǐ kàn kàn 。",
                "meaning": "Take a look; the verb repetition suggests a brief action.",
                "audio": "b7a6bf1d4966f039255174778d7c643183cde5a9bfdcbbdf76c186563e1a67ff"
              }
            ]
          },
